===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Each of the five [[digits]] on the end of the [[foot]].
# The [[equivalent]] [[part]] in an [[animal]].
#: {{hyponyms|en|hoof}}
# That part of a [[shoe]] or [[sock]] covering the toe.
# Something resembling a toe, especially at the bottom or extreme end of something.
#: {{lb|en|golf}} the extreme end of the head of a [[club]].
#: {{lb|en|hurling}} the end of a [[hurley]].
#: {{lb|en|cricket}} the [[tip]] of the [[bat]] farthest from the [[handle]]
#: {{lb|en|kayaking}} the [[bow]]; the front of the kayak.
#: {{lb|en|geology}} a [[bulbous]] [[protrusion]] at the front of a [[lava]] [[flow]] or [[landslide]].
# {{lb|en|dance|uncountable}} An advanced form of [[ballet]] primarily performed by women, wearing [[pointe shoe]]s.
# {{lb|en|automotive}} An [[alignment]] of the [[wheel]]s of a road [[vehicle]], either positive ([[toe in]]), meaning the wheels are closer together at the front than at the back, or negative ([[toe out]]), the other way round.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} The [[journal]], or [[pivot]], at the lower end of a revolving [[shaft]] or [[spindle]], which rests in a step.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A [[lateral]] [[projection]] at one end, or between the ends, of a piece, such as a [[rod]] or [[bolt]], by means of which it is moved.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A [[projection]] from the [[periphery]] of a revolving piece, acting as a [[cam]] to lift another piece.
# {{lb|en|carpentry}} The long side of an angled cut.
# The upper end of the [[bit]] (cutting edge) of an [[axehead]]; as opposed to the [[heel]] (lower end).
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[cameltoe]].
# {{lb|en|AU|NZ|slang|uncountable}} [[speed#Noun|Speed]], [[energy#Noun|energy]], [[vigor#Noun|vigor]].
#: {{ux|en|to have a lot of '''toe'''}}
# (figuratively) a person

